\title{distributions7: S7 Framework for Probability Distributions}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Probability distributions as objects, built on the S7 object system. Each distribution carries its density, distribution and quantile functions, a random generator, its moments and the exact derivatives of the log-likelihood up to the fourth order (and the fifth in closed form for some families) with respect to the parameters, the response and the parameters on the scale of their link functions. The package includes univariate and multivariate families, wrappers for zero inflation, zero adjustment, truncation, folding, transformation, fixed parameters and reparametrization, maximum likelihood fitting with fit_distrib() and a validation battery with check_distrib(). A distribution defined by its density alone receives numerical methods for every other quantity. Part of the 'statmodels7' toolkit.
